<div class="author-info">
<h1>面向智能汽车人机交互的多模态情感计算研究</h1>
<p>Research on Multimodal Emotion Computing for Human-Computer Interaction in Intelligent Vehicles</p>
<div style="margin-top: 20mm;">
<p>作者：李智春</p>
<p>指导教师：XXX 教授</p>
<p>专业名称：软件工程</p>
<p>研究方向：人工智能与人机交互</p>
<p>培养单位：吉林大学软件学院</p>
<p>论文提交日期：2024年X月</p>
<p>论文答辩日期：2024年X月</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<div class="abstract">
<div class="abstract-title">摘要</div>
<p>随着智能汽车技术的快速发展，人机交互已成为提升驾驶体验和安全性的关键因素。传统的车载交互系统主要依赖语音和触控，缺乏对驾驶员情感状态的感知能力，难以实现真正自然、智能的人机交互。本研究旨在构建一个面向智能汽车场景的多模态情感交互智能体，通过融合文本、语音、视觉和生理信号等多模态信息，实现对驾驶员情绪的精准识别，并将情绪作为注意力机制增强对驾驶员意图的理解，最终生成具有情感表达能力的智能体响应。</p>
<p>本研究的主要贡献包括：（1）提出了一种基于情感转变感知的多模态融合机制，借鉴CFN-ESA方法，能够捕捉驾驶员情绪的动态变化，提升情绪识别的准确性和实时性；（2）引入了多模态功能最大相关（MFMC）自监督学习框架，通过最大化多模态依赖性提高模型在预训练阶段的特征学习能力；（3）设计了多种融合策略（领导-跟随注意力、两阶段融合等），可根据不同场景选择最优的融合方式；（4）构建了情绪-意图联合理解机制，将识别出的情绪作为动态注意力权重，调制意图理解模块，实现情绪驱动的意图推理。</p>
<p>在技术实现上，本研究基于Transformer架构，采用BERT、Wav2Vec2.0、ResNet-50等预训练模型进行多模态特征提取，通过跨模态注意力机制和异步融合策略实现多模态信息的有效融合。系统采用层次化Agent AI架构，以LLM为认知核心，集成轻量化感知模型与情感生成模块，确保在车载平台资源受限环境下的实时性。</p>
<p>实验部分将在后续研究中完成，计划使用CMU-MOSEI、IEMOCAP、MPDB等公开数据集进行模型训练和评估，并参考《汽车智能座舱智能化水平测试与评价方法》团体标准，从感知能力、交互能力、服务能力三个维度构建评估体系。</p>
<p>本研究对推动智能座舱情感交互技术的发展、提升驾驶安全与用户体验具有重要的理论价值与应用前景，为智能汽车人机交互系统的情感计算提供了新的技术路径。</p>
<div class="keywords">
<p><span>关键词：</span>多模态情感计算；智能汽车；人机交互；注意力机制；情感识别</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<div class="abstract">
<div class="abstract-title">Abstract</div>
<p>With the rapid development of intelligent vehicle technology, human-computer interaction has become a key factor in improving driving experience and safety. Traditional in-vehicle interaction systems mainly rely on voice and touch, lacking the ability to perceive the driver's emotional state, making it difficult to achieve truly natural and intelligent human-computer interaction. This research aims to build a multimodal emotion interaction agent for intelligent vehicle scenarios, which integrates multimodal information such as text, voice, vision, and physiological signals to achieve accurate recognition of driver emotions, uses emotions as attention mechanisms to enhance the understanding of driver intentions, and finally generates agent responses with emotional expression capabilities.</p>
<p>The main contributions of this research include: (1) proposing an emotion-shift-aware multimodal fusion mechanism based on the CFN-ESA method, which can capture the dynamic changes of driver emotions and improve the accuracy and real-time performance of emotion recognition; (2) introducing a multimodal functional maximum correlation (MFMC) self-supervised learning framework to improve the feature learning ability of the model in the pre-training stage by maximizing multimodal dependencies; (3) designing multiple fusion strategies (leader-follower attention, two-stage fusion, etc.) to select the optimal fusion method according to different scenarios; (4) constructing an emotion-intention joint understanding mechanism that uses recognized emotions as dynamic attention weights to modulate the intention understanding module, achieving emotion-driven intention reasoning.</p>
<p>In terms of technical implementation, this research is based on the Transformer architecture, using pre-trained models such as BERT, Wav2Vec2.0, and ResNet-50 for multimodal feature extraction, and achieving effective fusion of multimodal information through cross-modal attention mechanisms and asynchronous fusion strategies. The system adopts a hierarchical Agent AI architecture with LLM as the cognitive core, integrating lightweight perception models and emotion generation modules to ensure real-time performance in resource-constrained in-vehicle platform environments.</p>
<p>The experimental part will be completed in subsequent research, planning to use public datasets such as CMU-MOSEI, IEMOCAP, and MPDB for model training and evaluation, and referring to the group standard "Test and Evaluation Methods for Intelligent Level of Automotive Intelligent Cockpit" to construct an evaluation system from three dimensions: perception ability, interaction ability, and service ability.</p>
<p>This research has important theoretical value and application prospects for promoting the development of intelligent cockpit emotion interaction technology and improving driving safety and user experience, providing a new technical path for emotion computing in intelligent vehicle human-computer interaction systems.</p>
<div class="keywords">
<p><span>Keywords:</span> Multimodal Emotion Computing; Intelligent Vehicle; Human-Computer Interaction; Attention Mechanism; Emotion Recognition</p>
</div>
</div>

